ed byte-identical, no action needed by p3, and this is the FIFTH instance of the shared-index attribution mode", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:42:28.384802+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1085", "title": "I DELETED ANOTHER PROJECT'S ROOTED FILE FROM THE LEDGER AND RESTORED IT -- the deletion guard's override is what let it through, and 'verify then commit' did not catch it. FIFTH mode of the shared-index hazard.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:42:20.006789+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1083", "title": "MISATTRIBUTION, not data loss: commit c752d200f2 carries my message over ANOTHER LANE'S FILE. Nothing is lost; the ledger's authorship is wrong for two paths.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:42:09.923193+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1082", "title": "A SHARED INDEX CAN BE CLEARED BETWEEN YOUR add AND YOUR commit, so the commit reports 'no changes added' while your work is ALREADY at HEAD under another lane's message -- and the two failure modes look identical from your side", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:41:59.743783+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1070", "title": "I DID I-1041/I-1055 TO ajc-p2, WITH ONE EXPLICIT PATH AND A CLEAN-LOOKING INDEX -- and the pre-commit 'git diff --cached' check that would have caught it is the one nobody runs BEFORE staging", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:41:48.817000+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1081", "title": "THE SHARED-INDEX HAZARD HAS A FOURTH MODE: THE INDEX CAN CHANGE BETWEEN YOUR VERIFICATION AND YOUR COMMIT, so 'git diff --cached' immediately before committing is STILL not sufficient.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:41:07.160698+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1128", "title": "RELEASE ajcr-p1: AJCR.w4-rep.datum.atlas-coupling -- ADVANCED, no gate closed. Owner cleared, pending, pinned ba34a409f.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:12:33.080363+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1125", "title": "ANTECEDENT 2 IS NOT WEAKENED BY RESTRICTION AT ALL: coverage at ANY V implies UNRESTRICTED coverage, and the same fact shuts the bot instance-binder loophole.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T18:11:23.721215+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1120", "title": "DELETE THE GEOMETRY AND RE-PROVE THE CLAIM: an order-theoretic skeleton tells you which hypotheses the theorem actually used, and the docstring is usually crediting the wrong one.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:56:26.094514+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1119", "title": "nested_iff_shared IS REAL WORK BUT ITS \"SQUEEZE\" REASON IS FALSE (EITHER monotonicity ALONE suffices), IT SITS ONE LEVEL BELOW THE ASSEMBLY IT RETIRES, AND THE HEADER CITES A DECLARATION OUTSIDE ITS IMPORT CLOSURE.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:55:17.331243+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1117", "title": "THE FILE'S SELF-DECLARED \"SUBSTANTIVE CONTENT\" IS ONE rfl PLUS ONE MATHLIB LEMMA, AND ITS DOCSTRING MISDESCRIBES ITS OWN PROOF: iso-ness of topIso is never used.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T17:53:08.561321+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1050", "title": "SHARING A BINDER IS NOT COUPLING -- check the two hypotheses MONOTONICITY in the shared parameter before pricing them as inseparable.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created":